# Line endings are load-bearing here.
#
# These files get downloaded straight to a device and run with /bin/sh. A CRLF
# ending makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r",
# and then every script fails with a confusing "not found" while looking
# perfectly fine in an editor. Pin LF for the repo and on checkout, whatever
# core.autocrlf happens to be set to locally.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
